        "original_id": "fd4ff1de-bc34-540b-9e2e-53fb12dc7d86",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mehdi Hashemi, Ronald Reagan\n- Events: Iran–Contra affair\n- Governments: United States, Reagan Administration, Iranian regime\n- Concepts: sedition, murder, opposition to secret dealings\n\nFacts:\n- The Iran–Contra affair, also called Irangate, Contragate, or the Iran–Contra scandal, was a political scandal in the United States during the second term of the Reagan Administration.\n- Mehdi Hashemi was officially found guilty of sedition, murder, and related charges.\n- Some people suspected that Mehdi Hashemi’s real offense was opposing the Iranian regime’s secret dealings with the United States connected to the Iran–Contra affair.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
